\section{Alabaster format, \code{AlabasterParam}}{


Calling \code{saveMsObject()} on a \code{MsBackendMetaboLights} with an
\code{AlabasterParam} parameter object stores the backend data in a directory
specified with parameter \code{path} of the parameter object. The stash folder
content is identical to the \link{MsBackendMzRStash} with only the class
definition of the \emph{OBJECT} file being specific for the stored backend class.

Restoring a \code{MsBackendMetaboLights} from the stash folder imports the
metadata and, if not available in the local cache, downloads the mass
spectrometry data files from the MetaboLights repository. Synchronizing
the locally cached data requires an active internet connection, even if no
data needs to be downloaded. Setting parameter \code{offline = TRUE} avoids the
synchronization, but requires the mass spectrometry data files to be
present in the local cache.

